EXT. THE LAST BRIDGE OF STARLIGHT, CLOUD CROSSING - TWILIGHT

A bridge of braided silver woven across a gulf of clouds. Far below, a sea of mist rolls over unseen mountains. Above, the first stars wink into a violet sky. At the midpoint of the span stands a gate of white stone, and before the gate waits a figure in a robe the color of fog.

WARDEN ISAURA MENDELSSOHN-OKAFOR (ageless, silver hair to her waist) rests both hands on a staff of pale wood. She does not move, though the wind tugs at her robe.

Two travelers approach along the bridge from the west: SIR BALTHAZAR OYELARAN-STIRLING (50s, battered plate armor, a laugh lurking behind a grim mouth), who limps, and a young mage, FENELLA CROSSLEY-AKINTOLA (20s, ink-stained sleeves, a spellbook the size of a paving stone), who walks backward half the time to check on him. They stop ten paces from the gate.

ISAURA
Travelers. State your purpose.

BALTHAZAR
We seek passage to the east, Warden.

FENELLA
(over him)
Not passage, exactly, it's more of a delivery --

BALTHAZAR
Fenella --

FENELLA
-- we have a message for the Moon Queen, you see, it's rather urgent --

ISAURA
The Queen receives no messages.

FENELLA
Not even this one?

BALTHAZAR
Especially this one.

FENELLA
(whispering, to Balthazar)
You're not helping.

BALTHAZAR
(whispering back)
I'm helping a great deal.

Isaura taps her staff once on the silver. A clear note rings out across the gulf. The clouds below shiver, the stars overhead pulse, and the gate swings inward a hand's breadth before stopping.

ISAURA
Three questions. Answer truly, and the gate opens. Answer falsely, and the bridge forgets you.

FENELLA
(swallowing)
Forgets us?

BALTHAZAR
It means we fall.

FENELLA
I know what it means!

ISAURA
First question. What do you carry?

BALTHAZAR
(simply)
A letter and a debt.

FENELLA
(at the same time)
A spellbook and an apology.

ISAURA
Second question. Whom do you fear?

FENELLA
The Queen.

BALTHAZAR
Myself.

Isaura's face does not change. But the staff trembles in her grip, ever so slightly.

ISAURA
Third question. What do you hope for?

Balthazar looks at Fenella. Fenella looks at Balthazar. A long silence stretches across the bridge, long enough for the first moon to rise, a pale silver coin over the clouds.

BALTHAZAR
That she reads it.

FENELLA
That she forgives it.

The gate opens fully. Isaura steps aside and bows her head, and the three of them stand in the starlight, the only people in the world.

ISAURA
Pass, then. And be kind to her.
